# Build Process

When building the application, always use the mise tasks defined in
[mise.toml](mdc:mise.toml). Do not invoke build commands directly; instead, run
the appropriate task with `mise run <task>` (e.g., `mise run build:all`). This
ensures all required steps and dependencies are handled consistently. List every
task with `mise tasks`.

## Examples

Below are some examples of how to run/test the application.

- Build the application: `mise run build:all` (runs cleanup, builds the web client (Lit + Vite) and backend (go))
- Run the application backend: `mise run run` (runs the web client and backend together for development)
- Test the application: `mise run test`
- Clean the application: `mise run clean`
- Clean and remove all build artifacts: `mise run clean:dist` (removes the `dist` directory)
- Clean web client build output: `mise run clean:web-client` (removes the `web-client/dist` directory)
- Install dependencies: `mise run deps` (go mod tidy plus bun installs for web client, TUI, and docs)
- Show all available tasks: `mise tasks`
